(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Attribution: cite this repository *and* the source publication of any record you rely on.
Every record carries `source.pmid` / `source.pmcid` / `source.doi` for that purpose.

## What these licences do NOT cover

Neither licence extends to the underlying publications. The extracted facts are ours to
license; the papers are not. Specifically:

- `Evidence.quote` is populated only for sources whose own licence permits redistributing
  expression (CC0 / CC BY / CC BY-SA). See `docs/LICENSING.md`.
- Records derived from sources under NonCommercial or NoDerivatives terms carry facts and
  character offsets only, with `quotes_permitted: false`.
- Records derived from sources outside the PMC Open Access subset are abstract-derived only.

Every record states its tier, so you can filter without re-deriving our reasoning.

